{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalkCompute","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalkCompute","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalkDegreeBound"],"declarations":78,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_hmStepZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_hmStepZ","kind":"theorem","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L768-L785","doc":"**One whole normal-form step scales.** `hmStepZ` denotes `cNum` times\n`hmStep`, so the scale relation is preserved by a step and accumulates across\nthe walk. `znorm` is transparent here by `denoteZ_znorm`.\n\nThis is the capstone of the scale chain: per table entry\n(`denoteZ_contribZ_scaled`), then across the fold (`denoteZ_foldl_scaled`),\nthen for the step. What remains purely mechanical is matching\n`nucleonStepsZ`/`interfaceStepZ` against `nucleonSteps`/`interfaceStep`\nentry by entry — each pair is one of the three `scaledStep_*` facts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_foldl_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_foldl_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":740,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L740-L766","doc":"**The step-level fold scales.** Accumulating the table's contributions\npreserves the scale relation, so one whole normal-form step does. This is the\ninduction that lifts `denoteZ_contribZ_scaled` from a single table entry to a\nstep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_contribZ_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_contribZ_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":703,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L703-L738","doc":"The scaled form of `denoteZ_contribZ`: if the input already carries a\nscale `k`, the output carries `cNum * k`. This is the shape the walk-level\ninduction needs, since the scale accumulates across steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_contribZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_contribZ","kind":"theorem","line":666,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L666-L701","doc":"**One table entry scales.** The integral contribution denotes `cNum` times\nthe rational one. This is the level at which `contribZ` and `contrib` differ,\nso it is the level the scale relation has to be proved at. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_half","kind":"theorem","line":664,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L664-L664","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_full","kind":"theorem","line":662,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L662-L662","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.scaledStep_zero","kind":"theorem","line":660,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L660-L660","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ScaledStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ScaledStep","kind":"def","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L655-L658","doc":"The integral multiplier pair `(cNum, dNum)` is the `cNum`-fold scaling of\nthe rational pair `(1, dRat)`. Holds for all three steps the atom path uses:\n`(1,0)/0`, `(1,-1)/(-1)`, and `(2,-1)/(-1/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_ne_neutron_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_ne_neutron_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":636,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L636-L642","doc":"**Proton and neutron are distinguished by the grading.** The corollary\nworth stating on its own: the two differ in q-degree, so the surviving\nGröbner–Shirshov grading separates them even though the numeric normal form\nat `q₀` gives both the same six-dimensional state space. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.neutron_terms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.neutron_terms","kind":"theorem","line":633,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L633-L634","doc":"Neutron term counts per coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_terms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_terms","kind":"theorem","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L629-L630","doc":"Proton term counts per coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.neutron_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.neutron_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":621,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L621-L626","doc":"**Neutron normal-form q-degrees.** The proton and the neutron differ —\na distinction the numeric normal form at `q₀` cannot express, since it\ncollapses every coefficient to a single float. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_degrees","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.proton_degrees","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L615-L618","doc":"**Proton normal-form q-degrees, computed from the braid word.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.termProfileZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.termProfileZ","kind":"def","line":594,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L594-L595","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.degreeProfileZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.degreeProfileZ","kind":"def","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L588-L592","doc":"The q-degree profile of the integer walk. Equal to the rational walk's,\nbecause the two differ by the nonzero scalar `2^k` and a nonzero scalar moves\nno exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNFZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNFZ","kind":"def","line":578,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L578-L586","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.interfaceStepZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.interfaceStepZ","kind":"def","line":573,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L573-L576","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nucleonStepsZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nucleonStepsZ","kind":"def","line":560,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L560-L571","doc":"The integral step list: `(cNum, dNum, dH, gen)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nfOneZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nfOneZ","kind":"def","line":558,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L558-L558","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStepZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStepZ","kind":"def","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L550-L556","doc":"One integral step, collected. `cNum` and `dNum` are the integral form of\nthe multiplier pair; `(1,0)`, `(1,-1)` and `(2,-1)` are the three the atom\npath uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.contribZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.contribZ","kind":"def","line":545,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L545-L548","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.NF6Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.NF6Z","kind":"def","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L543-L543","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_znorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_znorm","kind":"theorem","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L533-L539","doc":"**Integer normalisation preserves the denotation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zinsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zinsert","kind":"theorem","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L500-L531","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zmulH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zmulH","kind":"theorem","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L486-L498","doc":"The integer shift-and-negate denotes multiplication by `h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zsmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_zsmul","kind":"theorem","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L475-L484","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_append","kind":"theorem","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L466-L473","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.znorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.znorm","kind":"def","line":462,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L462-L464","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zinsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zinsert","kind":"def","line":456,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L456-L460","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zsmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zsmul","kind":"def","line":454,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L454-L454","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zmulH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.zmulH","kind":"def","line":451,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L451-L452","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_cons","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L448-L449","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ_nil","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L446-L446","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denoteZ","kind":"def","line":441,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L441-L444","doc":"What an integer term list denotes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ZLaurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ZLaurent","kind":"def","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L438-L439","doc":"A computable Laurent polynomial with **integer** coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.rawTerms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.rawTerms","kind":"def","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L414-L417","doc":"Raw term count of the walk, before collection: a computable upper bound on\nthe number of distinct monomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.termProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.termProfile","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L410-L412","doc":"Term count per coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.degreeProfile","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.degreeProfile","kind":"def","line":403,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L403-L408","doc":"The q-degree profile: the maximum exponent of each of the six\ncoefficients. Because the walk is collected at every step and\n`denote_cnorm` says collection preserves the denotation, these are the\nexponents of the polynomials the walk computes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNFN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNFN","kind":"def","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L392-L401","doc":"The atom normal form, collected at every step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.runStepsN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.runStepsN","kind":"def","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L388-L390","doc":"Run a list of steps, collecting after each. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_hmStepN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_hmStepN","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L383-L386","doc":"Normalising a step changes nothing about what it denotes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStepN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStepN","kind":"def","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L378-L381","doc":"One step, with the result collected. Denotes the same thing as `hmStep`\nby `denote_cnorm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cnorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cnorm","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L358-L368","doc":"**Normalisation preserves the denotation.**\n\nThis is what licenses reading a degree off `cnorm`: the collected list denotes\nthe same Laurent polynomial as the raw walk, so its exponents really are the\nexponents of the polynomial the walk computes, not an artefact of collection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cnorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cnorm","kind":"def","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L353-L356","doc":"Collect duplicate exponents and drop zero coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cinsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cinsert","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L320-L351","doc":"**Insertion denotes adding the term.** The cancellation branch is the one\nthat matters: dropping a term whose coefficients sum to zero does not change\nwhat the list denotes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cinsert","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cinsert","kind":"def","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L308-L318","doc":"Insert a single term into a list, combining it with any existing term at\nthe same exponent and dropping the result when it cancels.\n\nDefined by recursion rather than by grouping-and-summing, because each step is\nthen a small equation that `denote` can be pushed through — which is what\nmakes `denote_cinsert` provable at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.atomNF","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L283-L292","doc":"The full atom normal form, computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.runSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.runSteps","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L279-L281","doc":"Run a list of steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.interfaceStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.interfaceStep","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L273-L277","doc":"The interface step between two nucleons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nucleonSteps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nucleonSteps","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L260-L271","doc":"The step list for one nucleon: `(dRat, dH, gen)` triples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ordering.go","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ordering.go","kind":"def","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L253-L257","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ordering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.ordering","kind":"def","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L250-L258","doc":"Interleaved proton/neutron ordering, mirroring `_ground_state_ordering`.\n`true` is a proton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nfOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.nfOne","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L239-L240","doc":"The identity normal form, `q⁰` in the first basis slot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.hmStep","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L231-L237","doc":"One normal-form step: `nf ← nf · (σ_gen + d)` with `d = dRat · h^dH`.\nEvery multiplier used is `1`, `h`, or a rational times one of them — which is\nprecisely the hypothesis shape of `walk_mem_spanRange`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.contrib","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.contrib","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L225-L229","doc":"The contribution a single table entry makes, before it is accumulated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.table1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.table1","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L216-L223","doc":"Transfer table for generator `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.table0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.table0","kind":"def","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L207-L214","doc":"Transfer table for generator `σ₀`, as `(source, target, multiplier)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instReprMult.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instReprMult.repr","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instReprMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instReprMult","kind":"instance","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instDecidableEqMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.instDecidableEqMult","kind":"instance","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L205-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.d","kind":"ctor","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L204-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.ch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.ch","kind":"ctor","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L203-L203","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult.c","kind":"ctor","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.Mult","kind":"inductive","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L199-L205","doc":"Which multiplier a table entry carries: the identity `c = 1`, the product\n`c·h`, or the step's own coefficient `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.NF6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.NF6","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L196-L197","doc":"A normal-form state: six Laurent coefficients over the GS basis of `H₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cone","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L186-L187","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cmulH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cmulH","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L169-L184","doc":"**The load-bearing bridge lemma.** The computable shift-and-negate on\nexponents denotes multiplication by `h = q - q⁻¹`. This is what makes the\nexecutable walk a computation *of the abstract object* rather than a second,\nunverified program that happens to be written in Lean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_csmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_csmul","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L160-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cadd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cadd","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L157-L158","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_append","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L146-L155","doc":"Concatenation denotes the sum. Stated for `++` directly so it can be\nused to reason about `List.flatMap`, which produces appends. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cone","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L141-L142","doc":"The unit: `q⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.csmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.csmul","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L138-L139","doc":"Scaling by a rational coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cmulH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cmulH","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L132-L136","doc":"Multiplication by `h = q - q⁻¹` is a shift-and-negate on each term — the\ncomputable counterpart of `hQ_mul_T`, and the reason the walk is linear in the\nnumber of terms rather than quadratic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cadd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.cadd","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L128-L130","doc":"Addition is concatenation: no term collection is required for the sum to\nbe correct. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_cons","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L123-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote_nil","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.denote","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L116-L119","doc":"What a `CLaurent` denotes: the Laurent polynomial `∑ cᵢ · q^{eᵢ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.CLaurent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.LaurentWalk.CLaurent","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/LaurentWalkCompute.lean#L109-L114","doc":"A computable Laurent polynomial over `ℚ`: a list of `(exponent,\ncoefficient)` terms, understood as their sum. Duplicate exponents are\npermitted — normalisation is a separate operation, and imposing it as an\ninvariant would have to be re-established after every step for no gain in the\nsemantics. ","signatureChunk":0}]}